            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.086,
            0.898,
            0.118
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What does "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 \\mathrm { H } _ { 2 } \\mathrm { O }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " signify? Does it make "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { N a _ { 2 } C O _ { 3 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "wet? We will address this question in the next section.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.275,
            0.118,
            0.899,
            0.152
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sodium carbonate and sodium hydrogencarbonate are useful chemicals for many industrial processes as well.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.166,
            0.485,
            0.182
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Uses of washing soda"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.182,
            0.899,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Sodium carbonate (washing soda) is used in glass, soap and paper industries.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.214,
            0.897,
            0.23
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) It is used in the manufacture of sodium compounds such as borax.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.297,
            0.23,
            0.899,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Sodium carbonate can be used as a cleaning agent for domestic purposes.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.297,
            0.262,
            0.806,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) It is used for removing permanent hardness of water.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.294,
            0.714,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.4.4 Are the Crystals of Salts really Dry?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.076,
            0.323,
            0.509,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.076,
                0.323,
                0.509,
                0.583
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.075,
                0.596,
                0.203,
                0.64
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Figure 2.9 Removing water of crystallisation"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.542,
            0.33,
            0.714,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 2.15"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.534,
            0.365,
            0.875,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Heat a few crystals of copper sulphate in a dry boiling tube.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.535,
            0.394,
            0.876,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the colour of the copper sulphate after heating?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.537,
            0.423,
            0.876,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you notice water droplets in the boiling tube? Where have these come from?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.542,
            0.467,
            0.876,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Add 2-3 drops of water on the sample of copper sulphate obtained after heating.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.535,
            0.51,
            0.875,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you observe? Is the blue colour of copper sulphate restored?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.596,
            0.9,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Copper sulphate crystals which seem to be dry contain water of crystallisation. When we heat the crystals, this water is removed and the salt turns white.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.644,
            0.899,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If you moisten the crystals again with water, you will find that blue colour of the crystals reappears.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.676,
            0.9,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Water of crystallisation is the fixed number of water molecules present in one formula unit of a salt. Five water molecules are present in one formula unit of copper sulphate. Chemical formula for hydrated copper",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " sulphate is Cu "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{SO}_{4^{-}}^{-}\\mathrm{^{5}H_{2}O}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Now you would be able to answer the question",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " whether the molecule of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{Na_{2}CO_{3}.10H_{2}O}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "is wet.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.274,
            0.756,
            0.899,
            0.806
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "One other salt, which possesses water of crystallisation is gypsum. It has two water molecules as water of cyrstallisation. It has the chemical",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " formula "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "CaSO _{4} .2 H _{2} O"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ".",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let us look into the use of this salt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.812,
            0.432,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Plaster of Paris"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.275,
            0.828,
            0.899,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "On heating gypsum at 373 K, it loses water molecules and becomes",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.276,
            0.852,
            0.901,
            0.883
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "calcium sulphate hemihydrate "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( \\mathrm { C a S O } _ { 4 }   . \\frac { 1 } { 2 }   \\mathrm { H } _ { 2 } \\mathrm { O }   )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". This is called Plaster of",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.093,
            0.917,
            0.121,
            0.931
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "32"
            }
          ]
        },
